## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical observability and data reliability skills in a real-world, beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Beam Metrics and Cloud Monitoring integration
- Idempotent streaming writes with insertId
- Lightweight auditing and error handling
- Alerting on data quality metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-beam sketch (JavaScript/TypeScript syntax used for illustration)
class ParseEvent extends DoFn {
  @ProcessElement
  process(@Element json, output) {
    const event = JSON.parse(json.image);
    this.ingested.inc();
    // ... validation and transformation
    this.processed.inc();
    output(event);
  }

  @Setup
  setup() {
    this.ingested = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'ingested_events');
    this.processed = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'processed_events');
    this.failed = Metrics.counter('pipeline', 'failed_events');
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesss ability to design scalable, privacy-preserving streaming pipelines with per-tenant controls and lineage. It also tests cross-region delivery and data-exchange mechanics.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped masking and schema versioning
- Streaming ingestion: Pub/Sub + Dataflow
- Per-tenant partitioned analytics in BigQuery
- End-to-end lineage via Data Catalog; sharing via Data Exchange
- 24h per-tenant rollback using raw logs in Cloud Storage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow masking (simplified)
function maskPII(event) {
  event.email = hash(event.email).slice(0,8) + "@masked";
  // mask other PII fields
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollout and rollback for 24h per-tenant in production?
- How would you detect and handle schema drift across tenants/regions?
